  "notes": "Source: https://pennwest.catalog.acalog.com/mime/media/10/3438/BS+Biology+-+Pre-Med+Sci+202330.pdf (official PennWest Degree Planner, 2025-2026 Undergraduate Catalog, created 8/21/2023). Hand-transcribed 2026-09-30 from the Suggested Four Year Course Sequence. 120 credits total. Concentration: Pre-Medical Science (PMSC). Foundations (12): COMJ 1010, MATH 2320 or 2410, Technological Literacy, ENGL 1200. Discoveries (27): Art/Humanities 9cr, Social Sciences 9cr (incl. PSYC 1000), Natural Sciences & Technology 9cr (major lab sciences satisfy most; 4cr additional NS modeled). Required Major (47): BIOL 1400/1700/1900/2010 (or PHIL 3220)/2202/2810+2811/3810+3811/3326/3330; CHEM 1108/1128/2200+2205; PHYS 1500+1510/1600+1610. Related Electives (13): upper BIOL/CHEM incl. BIOL 4480/4951/4985/4999 (Keystone); modeled as BIOL 4999, BIOL 4480 + two upper electives. STAT 2020. Wellness (3). Free Electives (18). Program note: additional courses may be required for professional schools (e.g., English Comp II, additional Psychology/Sociology, Chemistry minor recommended). Prerequisites: CHEM 1108 -> CHEM 1128 -> CHEM 2200; BIOL 1400/1700/1900 sequence; PHYS 1500 -> PHYS 1600; BIOL 2810 -> BIOL 3810.",
